{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1021", "sample_idx": 17, "model_name": "qwen/qwen3-next-80b-a3b-instruct", "content": "PARAGRAPH 1  \nTHE SENTENCE \"IF THE LAW IS BAD, YOU SHOULD NOT FOLLOW IT\" IS OVERSIMPLIFIED AND POTENTIALLY DANGEROUS. IT IMPLIES A CLEAR, OBJECTIVE STANDARD FOR WHAT CONSTITUTES A “BAD” LAW, WHICH IS HIGHLY SUBJECTIVE AND VARIES ACROSS CULTURES, IDEOLOGIES, AND HISTORICAL CONTEXTS. WITHOUT A FRAMEWORK FOR DETERMINING HOW OR BY WHOM A LAW IS JUDGED “BAD,” THIS STATEMENT ENCOURAGES INDIVIDUAL ARBITRARINESS OVER COLLECTIVE ORDER. HISTORY SHOWS THAT DISREGARDING LAWS BASED ON PERSONAL MORALITY CAN LEAD TO CHAOS, ANARCHY, OR THE JUSTIFICATION OF TYRANNY—EVEN WHEN THE INDIVIDUAL BELIEVES THEY ARE RIGHT. THE SENTENCE FAILS TO ACKNOWLEDGE THE ROLE OF DEMOCRATIC PROCESSES, LEGAL REFORM, OR CIVIL DISOBEDIENCE AS STRUCTURED ALTERNATIVES TO BLIND NONCOMPLIANCE.\n\nPARAGRAPH 2  \nFURTHERMORE, THE SENTENCE IGNORES THE FOUNDATIONAL PRINCIPLE THAT LAWS, EVEN FLAWED ONES, SERVE AS THE STRUCTURAL BACKBONE OF SOCIETY. TO DECLARE THAT BAD LAWS SHOULD BE IGNORED IS TO UNDERMINE THE VERY IDEA OF THE RULE OF LAW, WHICH DEMANDS THAT ALL CITIZENS, INCLUDING THOSE WHO DISAGREE WITH THE LAW, SUBMIT TO ITS AUTHORITY UNTIL IT IS CHANGED THROUGH LEGITIMATE MEANS. THIS PHRASE LACKS NUANCE—IT DOES NOT DISTINGUISH BETWEEN CIVIL DISOBEDIENCE (PUBLIC, NONVIOLENT, AND CONSCIENTIOUS) AND SIMPLE LAWLESSNESS. IN A FUNCTIONING DEMOCRACY, THE RESPONSIBILITY TO CHANGE BAD LAWS LIES WITH THE COMMUNITY, NOT THE INDIVIDUAL ACTING IN ISOLATION. THE SENTENCE, IN ITS BLUNT FORM, IS NOT JUST INCOMPLETE—IT IS RECKLESS.", "logprobs": [{"token": "PAR", "logprob": -2.3841855067985307e-07}, {"token": "AGR", "logprob": -1.6093124941107817e-05}, {"token": "APH", "logprob": -8.344646857949556e-07}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -2.1576648578047752e-05}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "  \n", "logprob": -0.0059441933408379555}, {"token": "THE", "logprob": -0.007676506415009499}, {"token": " S